{"kind":"propose","text":"Correct the MCP selector trust description before implementation is finalized. Current generateActor provisioning calls ed25519.GenerateKey with randomness; cryptographic key material is not derived from the actor name. The actor name selects configuration and a per-name key file, and development provisioning automatically creates a random key there. Because one OS account can usually read every repository actor key, actor separation is operational rather than an access boundary until filesystem or secret custody restricts which keys the adapter can open. Keep the requested selector behavior: select repository first; select an existing configured actor key only; load it once per call; verify its public fingerprint against configuration and a live participant roster row; hard-refuse missing, unreadable, mismatched, retired, nonparticipant, unknown, empty, or wrong-typed selection without fallback; key resident credential, inbox, notice, and presence state by common repository identity plus selected actor. Document point-in-time per-call custody and the future access-gated boundary. Never derive a key path directly or mint during selection. Ratify this correction to replace the request phrase that says the development key model derives keys from actor names; do not change the remaining conditions."}